From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/setup: constrain pip to 24.3.1

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 wheel availability: pip 23.2.1 lists no manylinux_*_riscv64 tags, so it can't install any riscv64 wheel]

Pigweed's virtualenv setup upgrades the bootstrap venv's pip under
CHIP's constraints.txt, which pins pip==23.2.1. That pip vendors
packaging 21.3, whose manylinux arch allowlist has no riscv64, so on a
riscv64 host it reports only linux_riscv64 tags and treats every
manylinux_*_riscv64 wheel as incompatible. With cryptography taken as a
binary only (patch 0004, PIP_ONLY_BINARY), pip then finds no candidate
for cryptography==43.0.1, even though pypi.riseproject.dev serves it as
cp39-abi3-manylinux_2_35_riscv64, and the install of the generated
`pigweed` package fails with ResolutionImpossible.

pip 24.1 is the first release whose vendored packaging (24.1) lists
riscv64. Pin 24.3.1, the version this Pigweed revision's own
python_base_requirements.txt pins and the one it already installs in
the GN build venv, which ignores constraints.txt for that step.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 scripts/setup/constraints.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/setup/constraints.txt b/scripts/setup/constraints.txt
index 89cd541..2a95ba8 100644
--- a/scripts/setup/constraints.txt
+++ b/scripts/setup/constraints.txt
@@ -277,7 +277,7 @@ wheel==0.38.4 ; sys_platform == "linux"
     #   pip-tools

 # The following packages are considered to be unsafe in a requirements file:
-pip==23.2.1
+pip==24.3.1
     # via
     #   fastcore
     #   ghapi
--
2.50.1
